##### MF1: GENERAL INFORMATION                                    8325 1451  222
                                                                  8325 1451  223
- MT451    : Descriptive data and directory                       8325 1451  224
                                                                  8325 1451  225
This text and the full directory of used MF/MT sections.          8325 1451  226
                                                                  8325 1451  227
##### MF2: RESONANCE PARAMETERS                                   8325 1451  228
                                                                  8325 1451  229
- MT151    : Resonance parameters                                 8325 1451  230
                                                                  8325 1451  231
Details about the origin of the resonance parameters for this     8325 1451  232
nuclide are given above in this description. In general, both a   8325 1451  233
Resolved and an Unresolved Resonance Range are given.             8325 1451  234
                                                                  8325 1451  235
##### MF3: REACTION CROSS SECTIONS                                8325 1451  236
                                                                  8325 1451  237
All the data present in the following MT-sections have been       8325 1451  238
calculated with TALYS, possibly normalized to experimental data.  8325 1451  239
If the maximal cross section in an excitation function over the   8325 1451  240
whole energy range does not exceed 1.e-9 b, the MT-number is not  8325 1451  241
included. Cross sections lower than 1.e-20 b are assumed to have  8325 1451  242
no physical meaning and are set to zero. All MT numbers extend up 8325 1451  243
to the highest incident energy.                                   8325 1451  244
The following reaction channels/MT numbers are generally included:8325 1451  245
                                                                  8325 1451  246
- MT1      : Total cross section                                  8325 1451  247
                                                                  8325 1451  248
Calculated with the optical model over the whole energy range,    8325 1451  249
or partly reproduced using experimental data.                     8325 1451  250
                                                                  8325 1451  251
- MT2      : Elastic scattering cross section                     8325 1451  252
                                                                  8325 1451  253
Obtained by subtracting the non-elastic cross section from the    8325 1451  254
total cross section.                                              8325 1451  255
                                                                  8325 1451  256
- MT3      : Non-elastic cross section                            8325 1451  257
                                                                  8325 1451  258
Calculated with the optical model over the whole energy range.    8325 1451  259
                                                                  8325 1451  260
- MT4      : Total inelastic cross section                        8325 1451  261
                                                                  8325 1451  262
Sum of MT=51-91.                                                  8325 1451  263
                                                                  8325 1451  264
- MT5      : (n,anything) cross section                           8325 1451  265
                                                                  8325 1451  266
MT5 contains the reactions which can not be stored in any other   8325 1451  267
MT-number. The information of MF3/MT5 can be combined with        8325 1451  268
MF6/MT5 to obtain residual production cross sections particle     8325 1451  269
production cross sections and (double-)differential cross         8325 1451  270
sections.                                                         8325 1451  271
                                                                  8325 1451  272
- MT16     : (n,2n) cross section                                 8325 1451  273
- MT17     : (n,3n) cross section                                 8325 1451  274
- MT22     : (n,na) cross section                                 8325 1451  275
- MT28     : (n,np) cross section                                 8325 1451  276
- MT51-90  : (n,n') cross section for 1st-40th excited state      8325 1451  277
- MT91     : (n,n') continuum cross section                       8325 1451  278
- MT102    : (n,gamma) cross section                              8325 1451  279
- MT103    : (n,p) cross section                                  8325 1451  280
- MT104    : (n,d) cross section                                  8325 1451  281
- MT105    : (n,t) cross section                                  8325 1451  282
- MT106    : (n,h) cross section                                  8325 1451  283
- MT107    : (n,a) cross section                                  8325 1451  284
- MT600-610: (n,p) cross section for 0th-10th excited state       8325 1451  285
- MT649    : (n,p) continuum cross section                        8325 1451  286
- MT650-655: (n,d) cross section for 0th-5th excited state        8325 1451  287
- MT699    : (n,d) continuum cross section                        8325 1451  288
- MT700-705: (n,t) cross section for 0th-5th excited state        8325 1451  289
- MT749    : (n,t) continuum cross section                        8325 1451  290
- MT750-755: (n,h) cross section for 0th-5th excited state        8325 1451  291
- MT799    : (n,h) continuum cross section                        8325 1451  292
- MT800-810: (n,a) cross section for 0th-10th excited state       8325 1451  293
- MT849    : (n,a) continuum cross section                        8325 1451  294
                                                                  8325 1451  295
##### MF4: ANGULAR DISTRIBUTIONS OF SECONDARY PARTICLES           8325 1451  296
                                                                  8325 1451  297
We use MF4 for the neutron scattering angular distribution for    8325 1451  298
discrete levels.                                                  8325 1451  299
                                                                  8325 1451  300
- MT2      : Elastic angular distribution                         8325 1451  301
                                                                  8325 1451  302
The flag LTT=3 is used to indicate a switch at some high energy,  8325 1451  303
generally 50 MeV, from a Legendre representation to a tabulated   8325 1451  304
representation. For incident energies below this energy, the      8325 1451  305
Legendre coefficients are given on a sufficiently precise energy  8325 1451  306
grid. They are a sum of calculated Legendre coefficients for      8325 1451  307
compound nucleus and shape-elastic scattering. For higher         8325 1451  308
incident energies, relative angular distributions are tabulated   8325 1451  309
on an angular grid.                                               8325 1451  310
                                                                  8325 1451  311
- MT51-70  : (n,n') angular distribution for 1st-20th state       8325 1451  312
- MT600-610: (n,p) angular distribution for 0th-10th state        8325 1451  313
- MT650-655: (n,d) angular distribution for 0th-5th state         8325 1451  314
- MT700-705: (n,t) angular distribution for 0th-5th state         8325 1451  315
- MT750-755: (n,h) angular distribution for 0th-5th state         8325 1451  316
- MT800-810: (n,a) angular distribution for 0th-10th state        8325 1451  317
                                                                  8325 1451  318
##### MF6: PRODUCT ENERGY-ANGLE DISTRIBUTIONS                     8325 1451  319
                                                                  8325 1451  320
In MF6 we store all secondary energy, angle, and energy-angle     8325 1451  321
distributions, as well as all residual and discrete + continuum   8325 1451  322
photon production cross sections for channels other than capture  8325 1451  323
(MT102) and reactions to discrete levels (MT51,etc.).             8325 1451  324
All data are generated with TALYS.                                8325 1451  325
                                                                  8325 1451  326
- MT5      : (n,anything) yields and energy-angle distributions   8325 1451  327
                                                                  8325 1451  328
MT5 contains, in this order,                                      8325 1451  329
For neutrons up to alpha particles and photons:                   8325 1451  330
- the production yields per particle for the whole energy range   8325 1451  331
- the secondary energy-angle distributions per particles which are8325 1451  332
  not represented by explicit MT numbers. On a secondary energy   8325 1451  333
  grid the relative emission spectra are given together with the  8325 1451  334
  parameters for the Kalbach systematics for angular              8325 1451  335
  distributions. Inelastic scattering cross sections for discrete 8325 1451  336
  states have been broadened and added to the continuum spectra.  8325 1451  337
For each residual product:                                        8325 1451  338
- the production yields for the whole energy range.               8325 1451  339
- the recoil                                                      8325 1451  340
These distributions can be multiplied with MF3/MT5 to get         8325 1451  341
the production cross sections and (double-)differential cross     8325 1451  342
sections.                                                         8325 1451  343
                                                                  8325 1451  344
- MT16     : (n,2n) energy-angle distr. and photon production     8325 1451  345
                                                                  8325 1451  346
First, for each type of outgoing particle, the (trivial) integer  8325 1451  347
particle yields are given. Next, on a sufficiently dense incident 8325 1451  348
energy grid the secondary energy-angle distributions are          8325 1451  349
specified by means of the relative emission spectra and the       8325 1451  350
parameters for the Kalbach systematics for angular distributions. 8325 1451  351
Next, the photon yield is tabulated as a function of incident     8325 1451  352
energy. For each incident energy, the photon production is given  8325 1451  353
for all discrete gamma lines present in the final nucleus. A      8325 1451  354
continuum photon distribution is added to this. We assume         8325 1451  355
isotropy for all produced gamma rays.                             8325 1451  356
                                                                  8325 1451  357
For the following MT-numbers, the same procedure as for MT16 is   8325 1451  358
followed:                                                         8325 1451  359
                                                                  8325 1451  360
- MT17 : (n,3n) energy-angle distr. and photon production         8325 1451  361
- MT22 : (n,na) energy-angle distr. and photon production         8325 1451  362
- MT28 : (n,np) energy-angle distr. and photon production         8325 1451  363
- MT91 : (n,n') continuum energy-angle distr. and phot. prod.     8325 1451  364
- MT649: (n,p) continuum energy-angle distr. and photon prod.     8325 1451  365
- MT699: (n,d) continuum energy-angle distr. and photon prod.     8325 1451  366
- MT749: (n,t) continuum energy-angle distr. and photon prod.     8325 1451  367
- MT809: (n,h) continuum energy-angle distr. and photon prod.     8325 1451  368
- MT849: (n,a) continuum energy-angle distr. and photon prod.     8325 1451  369
                                                                  8325 1451  370
##### MF8: RADIOACTIVE DECAY DATA                                 8325 1451  371
                                                                  8325 1451  372
For reactions to isomers, MF8 designates where the information    8325 1451  373
for isomeric versus ground state production, or residual          8325 1451  374
production can be found, i.e. for each MT number it points to     8325 1451  375
either MF6, MF9 or MF10.                                          8325 1451  376
                                                                  8325 1451  377
##### MF9: MULTIPLICITIES FOR PRODUCTION OF RADIOACTIVE NUCLIDES  8325 1451  378
                                                                  8325 1451  379
MF9 is used for isomer production by non-threshold reactions.     8325 1451  380
Final states with a lifetime that exceeds 1 second are treated    8325 1451  381
as isomer.                                                        8325 1451  382
                                                                  8325 1451  383
##### MF10: CROSS SECTIONS FOR PRODUCTION OF RADIOACTIVE NUCLIDES 8325 1451  384
                                                                  8325 1451  385
MF10 is used for isomer production by threshold reactions.        8325 1451  386
Final states with a lifetime that exceeds 1 second are treated    8325 1451  387
as isomer.                                                        8325 1451  388
                                                                  8325 1451  389
##### MF12: PHOTON PRODUCTION YIELD DATA                          8325 1451  390
                                                                  8325 1451  391
MF12 is used for the photon production for two types of reactions:8325 1451  392
- Reactions to discrete levels (MT51, etc.) For this transition   8325 1451  393
  probabilities are used (LO=2)                                   8325 1451  394
- Photons from neutron capture (MT102). Here multiplicities are   8325 1451  395
  given                                                           8325 1451  396
                                                                  8325 1451  397
##### MF14: PHOTON ANGULAR DISTRIBUTIONS                          8325 1451  398
                                                                  8325 1451  399
All photon production is considered as isotropic                  8325 1451  400
                                                                  8325 1451  401
##### MF15: PHOTON ENERGY SPECTRA                                 8325 1451  402
                                                                  8325 1451  403
For capture (MT102), the photon energy spectrum is given.         8325 1451  404
                                                                  8325 1451  405
##### MF32: COVARIANCES OF RESONANCE PARAMETERS                   8325 1451  406
                                                                  8325 1451  407
In MF32, we store the covariances of resonance parameters,        8325 1451  408
and more details are given above in this description. In most     8325 1451  409
versions of TENDL, this information is now stored in MF33.        8325 1451  410
                                                                  8325 1451  411
##### MF33: COVARIANCES OF NEUTRON CROSS SECTIONS                 8325 1451  412
                                                                  8325 1451  413
In MF33, we store the covariances of most, but not all, reaction  8325 1451  414
channels that are given in MF3. All covariances are generated     8325 1451  415
with the TASMAN code [kon19], which generates TALYS runs using    8325 1451  416
a Monte Carlo parameter method.                                   8325 1451  417
For each MT-number, the information consists of:                  8325 1451  418
1. Covariances for MTa, Ea and MTa, Ea (variances)                8325 1451  419
2. Covariances for MTa, Ea and MTa, Eb (correlations for the      8325 1451  420
   same reaction channel between different energies)              8325 1451  421
3. Covariances for MTa, Ea and MTb, Ea (correlations between      8325 1451  422
   different reaction channels for the same energy)               8325 1451  423
4. Covariances for MTa, Ea and MTb, Eb (correlations between      8325 1451  424
   different reaction channels for different energies)            8325 1451  425
Classes 1 and 2 are covered by NI-type subsubsections with        8325 1451  426
flag LB=5, followed by a LB=8 section which contains              8325 1451  427
the cross section variances multiplied by 1.e-3. Next, classes 3  8325 1451  428
and 4 are covered by flag LB=6 to account for the different       8325 1451  429
energy grids that two correlating MT-sections may have. Since     8325 1451  430
the total correlation matrix is fully symmetric, we only need to  8325 1451  431
include the correlation elements between different MT-numbers     8325 1451  432
once, and we do that in the subsection with the lowest of the     8325 1451  433
two MT-numbers. We include covariance information for all the     8325 1451  434
total cross sections, the lumped partial cross sections and the   8325 1451  435
individual inelastic cross sections per level (MT51,...). We do   8325 1451  436
not include covariances for MT600 and higher MT-numbers. For the  8325 1451  437
most important channels, we include cross-channel correlations.   8325 1451  438
                                                                  8325 1451  439
##### MF34: COVARIANCES OF ANGULAR DISTRIBUTIONS                  8325 1451  440
                                                                  8325 1451  441
In MF34, we store the covariances of the elastic scattering       8325 1451  442
angular distributions that are given in MF4/MT2. All covariances  8325 1451  443
are generated with the TASMAN code [kon19], which generates       8325 1451  444
TALYS runs using a Monte Carlo parameter method. The tables are   8325 1451  445
restricted to MT2 and contain covariances for the first 6         8325 1451  446
Legendre coefficients. Both intra- and inter-correlations of the  8325 1451  447
various Legendre coefficients are given. As in MF33, the LB5      8325 1451  448
representation is used.                                           8325 1451  449
                                                                  8325 1451  450
##### MF40: COVARIANCES OF ISOMER PRODUCTION                      8325 1451  451
                                                                  8325 1451  452
For covariances of ground state and isomeric cross sections, the  8325 1451  453
same procedures as for MF33 are used.                             8325 1451  454
                                                                  8325 1451  455
